{
  "id": "Compound::DB00674 - Gene::1142",
  "verbalization": "Galantamine is implicated in the regulation of acetylcholine-activated cation-selective channel activity through its interaction with specific proteins, which are part of a broader network of molecular mechanisms involving ion channels. The evidence suggests that Galantamine binds to proteins such as Chrng, Chrne, and Chrna5, all of which participate in the same biological process—acetylcholine-activated cation-selective channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Chrnb3, indicating a potential role for these proteins in the functional expression of Chrnb3. The cumulative evidence from the three paths highlights a shared pathway where Galantamine's interactions with these proteins contribute to the activation of a channel that is associated with Chrnb3. The integration of these findings suggests that Galantamine may influence the function of Chrnb3 through its involvement in the regulation of ion channels, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
